      <title>Arsenal hold on for vital win at Liverpool after Kai Havertz’s close-range finish</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/01/liverpool-arsenal-premier-league-match-report</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;It was a game when Arsenal showed their ruthless side and all of the champion knowhow that they accumulated over the course of last season. As they headed back to London, they did so having made a statement. Irrespective of what happens to Manchester City over their financial rule breaches, Arsenal remain the Premier League’s team to beat.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mikel Arteta was in the Arsenal midfield when the club previously won a league fixture at Anfield; it was back in September 2012, although his memories are a little hazy owing to the concussion that he sustained in a collision with Jordan Henderson.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/01/liverpool-arsenal-premier-league-match-report"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
