      <title>Michael Carrick to stay in charge of Manchester United for Roma game</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/01/michael-carrick-stay-manager-manchester-united-roma-game</link>
      <description>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;United 17th in Premier League after Chelsea defeat&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;No change expected until international break&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Michael Carrick is poised to remain in charge of Manchester United for the Champions League game against Roma at Old Trafford on Tuesday despite &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/chelsea-manchester-united-premier-league-match-report"&gt;the 2-0 defeat&lt;/a&gt; at Chelsea on Saturday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;United have not won in nine games and have made their poorest start to a season since 1988, but Carrick’s position is expected to be reviewed again during the international break after the next round of Premier League matches, in which United host Aston&amp;nbsp;Villa next Sunday.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/01/michael-carrick-stay-manager-manchester-united-roma-game"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
