      <description>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Coventry fan, 14, had photo of Lowery at Coventry game&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bradley died aged six in 2017 with rare form of cancer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;A 14-year-old boy has “handed himself in” to West Midlands police after a video posted on social media appeared to show a Coventry fan taunting Sunderland with a photo of Bradley Lowery during the &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/coventry-sunderland-premier-league-match-report"&gt;Premier League match on Saturday&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sunderland fan Bradley captured the hearts of the football world when he was diagnosed with neuroblastoma, a rare form of childhood cancer. He died aged six in 2017.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/01/police-bradley-lowery-taunt-coventry-sunderland-premier-league"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
